 "result": "All of this is in `src/tessel/views.py`.\n\n- **`View.to_view_func(name, ...)`** (L86, classmethod) builds the view function.\n  - It defines an inner `view(**kwargs)` that instantiates the class (per request, unless `init_every_request` is `False`) and calls `self.run_view` via `active_app.ensure_sync` (L104-116).\n  - It applies any `decorators`, then attaches `view_class`, `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` to the function (L118-135). `attach_route_rule` reads these.\n- **`VerbView`** (L138) is the subclass that does the per-method routing.\n  - **`VerbView.__init_subclass__`** (L165) sets `cls.methods` automatically from the `get`/`post`/… methods defined on the class (and its bases), as uppercase names. It uses `http_method_funcs`, so those methods get registered with the route.\n  - **`VerbView.run_view`** (L182) does the dispatch: `getattr(self, request.method.lower())`. `HEAD` falls back to `get` if there is no `head`. It then calls the handler through `ensure_sync` with the URL kwargs.\n\nUsage: `app.attach_route_rule(\"/x\", view_func=MyView.to_view_func(\"x\"))`.",
